Minimum categories:

Security - Leakage or Unathorized Data Access. AI logs and model inputs/outputs may contain sensitive enterprise data; unauthorized access or inadvertent exposure during training or storage. Breach of customer confidentiality, regulatory violations (HIPAA, PCI DSS), reputational damage, legal liability. The impact is High. Implement logging controls with option to disable data storage; enhance strict adherence to permissions aligned with Box access policies; encrypt data in transit and at rest; conduct regular access audits. Risk Owner = Chief Information Security Officer (CISO) / Data Security Lead.
Privacy - Excessive Data Collection Beyond Necessity. Box AI systems may collect, retain, or transmit more customer data than strictly necessary for the intended AI function, violating data minimization principles. Increased breach surface area, regulatory non-compliance with GDPR and CCPA data minimization requirements, unnecessary exposure of sensitive information. The impact is High. Enforce strict data minimization policies limiting collection to data strictly necessary for AI functionality; implement automated data purging schedules; restrict retention windows for question-and-answer logs; conduct regular data audits to identify and eliminate unnecessary collection; document justification for every data element retained. Risk Owner = Data Protection Officer / Privacy Engineering Team.
Compliance - Inadequate Audit Trail & Documentation for Regulatory Investigations. Box AI may lack sufficient logging, audit trails, and documentation of AI decision-making, data usage, and compliance controls, making it difficult to demonstrate compliance during regulatory investigations or litigation. Regulatory enforcement escalation, inability to prove compliance posture, loss of Safe Harbor defenses, higher penalties, reputational damage from failed audits. The impact is High. Implement comprehensive logging and audit trail infrastructure capturing all AI processing, data access, consent decisions, and model changes; retain audit logs for minimum duration required by applicable regulations; establish automated compliance reporting and evidence collection mechanisms; conduct regular audits simulating regulatory investigations; maintain compliance documentation repository accessible to auditors; establish procedures for rapid evidence production in regulatory investigations. Risk Owner = Chief Information Security Officer / Compliance Officer.
Third Party - Vendor Non-Compliance with Security & Privacy Standards. AI service providers may fail to meet contractual security, data protection, or audit requirements; non-compliance may go undetected if monitoring is inadequate, cascading compliance failures to Box. Regulatory violations and fines imposed on Box due to vendor non-compliance, audit findings, inability to remediate compliance gaps, regulatory enforcement action. The impact is Medium. Conduct comprehensive compliance assessments of all AI providers covering GDPR, CCPA, HIPAA, PCI DSS, SOC 2, ISO 27001, and industry-specific standards; require vendors to maintain current certifications and attestations; establish continuous compliance monitoring with quarterly or semi-annual audits; implement automated compliance questionnaires and attestation refresh cycles; require vendors to disclose material compliance changes or incidents; establish incident response procedures for vendor non-compliance; include compliance breach remediation timelines and penalties in vendor contracts. Risk Owner = Chief Compliance Officer / Chief Information Security Officer.
Data Protection - Inadequate Access Controls and Privilege. Users may have access to more data than required for their role; inadequate access controls allow unauthorized data access, and insufficient monitoring enables privilege escalation attacks. Unauthorized data access by employees or attackers, insider theft of intellectual property or customer data, regulatory violations, data breaches. The impact is High. Implement Least Privilege (AC-6) access policies ensuring users only access data necessary for their role; deploy role-based access controls (RBAC) with granular permission management; enforce Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA) to reduce risk of account compromise; conduct regular access reviews and recertifications to validate appropriateness; implement privileged access management (PAM) for administrative accounts; monitor for anomalous access patterns indicating privilege escalation; maintain audit logs of all data access; establish automated alerts for unauthorized access attempts. Risk Owner = Chief Information Security Officer / Identity & Access Management Team.
Human Oversight - Undefined Oversight Responsibilities & Authority Gaps. Organizational roles and responsibilities for Box AI oversight may be unclear; ownership of oversight decisions, accountability for failures, and escalation authority remain ambiguous. Regulatory liability gaps, failures to escalate critical issues, lack of accountability when oversight fails, organizational confusion about who bears responsibility. The impact is Medium. Establish clear Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) defining oversight responsibilities by role and organizational level; document decision-making authority and escalation procedures; assign explicit accountability for monitoring, investigation, and override decisions; establish governance committees with clear mandates; conduct regular reviews validating that roles remain appropriately staffed and trained; establish clear communication channels enabling escalation of concerns. Risk Owner = Chief AI Officer / Chief Operating Officer.
Operational Risk - Monitoring & Alerting Gaps. Operational issues may not be detected promptly due to inadequate monitoring, alerting infrastructure, or alert fatigue; delayed detection extends incident duration and impact. Extended service disruptions, delayed incident response, increased customer impact, regulatory violations, higher incident remediation costs, ability to prevent ongoing issues. The impact is Medium. Implement comprehensive monitoring covering all critical systems, APIs, and performance metrics; establish automated alerting with appropriate thresholds and escalation procedures; implement alert tuning reducing false positives and alert fatigue; conduct quarterly monitoring assessments validating coverage and effectiveness; maintain 24/7 security operations center (SOC) monitoring critical systems; establish incident response procedures enabling rapid investigation; conduct post-incident reviews validating monitoring and alerting performed as expected. Risk Owner = Chief Information Security Officer / Security Operations Center.
Reputational Risk - Regulatory Enforcement Actions & Fines. Box AI practices may violate applicable regulations (GDPR, CCPA, AI-specific rules); resulting regulatory investigations, fines, or enforcement actions create immediate reputational damage and media coverage. Regulatory fines and penalties, mandatory operational changes, negative media coverage, loss of customer trust, stock price impact, regulatory scrutiny affecting future product development, years-long recovery. The impact is Medium. Maintain proactive compliance monitoring and regulatory engagement preventing violations; implement governance ensuring compliance with applicable regulations; establish regulatory relationships enabling early disclosure of potential issues; prepare crisis communications for potential regulatory enforcement actions; maintain legal resources enabling rapid response to regulatory investigations; conduct scenario-based planning for potential enforcement outcomes. Risk Owner = Chief Legal Officer / Chief Compliance Officer.

